From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:16:55 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] flashnext cuda: a rollback's replay in three launches
 (TF_FLASHNEXT_ROLL_BATCH)

TF_FLASHNEXT_ROLL_BATCH=1 runs a partial keep's replay as fn_replay_front, fn_replay_chain and fn_late_roll over
every DeltaNet layer at once (blockIdx.z the layer), the lone launches' programs on their own slices, so the state
and conv windows come out bit for bit as the per-layer loop leaves them. Default off.

From qwen-flash-rtx6000-tensorfold 0069, adapted to main's one-engine layer loop (no pipeline stage span); that
patch's TF_FLASHNEXT_SPIN_WAIT (rank waits at --tp 2 / --pp 2) is left out of this one-GPU series.
